the partition equilibrium. To separate the phases, centrifugation was done at 3000 × g for 5 min. The aqueous layer was carefully separated from the octanol layer for platinum analysis. Pt was quantified from aliquots taken from the octanol-saturated aqueous samples before and after partition by FAAS. Partition coefficients of Pt complexes were calculated using the equation log P = log ([Pt]WSO/[Pt]OSW)."}],"melting_points":[{"temperature_c":"158.4–159.3","event":"Melting point","Counterion":"","source":"10.1016/j.ejmech.2026.119066","source_page":"SI §7.1","notes":"Compound 3; Synthesis of Pt(IV) complex 3","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ejmech.2026.119066"}]}